# S5-07 `norandmaps` diagnostic N=2, 2026-11-15

Purpose: check whether disabling Linux address-space randomization changes the
run-to-run startup-stack page-fault count observed in earlier S5-07 diagnostics.
This is a diagnostic profile only, not acceptance evidence.

## Source and inputs

- Worktree/branch: `codex`; source revision `886f7fa57164ac82ebb198abb08bb05a72d4ab57`, clean.
- Host: macOS 26.7.1, arm64.
- Runner: release `target/release/od-runner`, SHA-256
  `90c5db937de8fff1501c1ce24f0b3a35a546b557dbe24c5a73bd24be6d6b343f`.
- Kernel SHA-256: `9f55ef7253055a9cf68f8a04323c93dead2fca617386d842fbde9ca7b178b27e`.
- Initramfs SHA-256: `ee9183a4eded3c16a8c6a7a81c6d5bb79be8bb023f793f7cd61694ea2bd3e588`.
- ACPI blob SHA-256: `b1ba6078a4d9bc7a8d224980713d8242e4a708743ce4f56093b00a07c631ffaf`.
- ACPI manifest SHA-256: `2bd690ae0817705b1b128675f9628dd7212fee74ab97c88da3599a1ae8e398f2`.
- Profile: `--run --budget 3000000000 --set-cpl0 --cpuid-profile stage4a
  --user-mode --linux-norandmaps`, 128 MiB. The runner appends `norandmaps`
  after `nokaslr`; both runs record `acceptance: diagnostic_not_counted`.

## Command

```sh
target/release/od-runner linux-direct --test-runs 2 \
  --series-id stage5-s5-07-stage4a-norandmaps-20261115-a \
  --scenario-id stage4-init-nonce \
  --expected-stop-kind budget_exhausted \
  --out work/stage5/stage5-s5-07-stage4a-norandmaps-20261115-a/series.json \
  --vmlinuz /Users/senya/projects/open_desktop/work/stage4/linux-7.0.0-38.38/vmlinuz-7.0.0-38-generic \
  --initramfs /Users/senya/projects/open_desktop/work/stage4/initramfs/initramfs.cpio \
  --acpi-blob tests/fixtures/guest/stage4/acpi_blob/stage4_acpi_blob.bin \
  --expected-vmlinuz-sha256 9f55ef7253055a9cf68f8a04323c93dead2fca617386d842fbde9ca7b178b27e \
  --expected-initramfs-sha256 ee9183a4eded3c16a8c6a7a81c6d5bb79be8bb023f793f7cd61694ea2bd3e588 \
  --expected-acpi-manifest-hash 2bd690ae0817705b1b128675f9628dd7212fee74ab97c88da3599a1ae8e398f2 \
  --ram-mib 128 --run --budget 3000000000 --set-cpl0 \
  --cpuid-profile stage4a --user-mode --linux-norandmaps
```

## Results

Both runs loaded Linux, passed exact nonce validation and reached
`retired=2,999,999,998` with `budget_exhausted`. Both had 1,093 CPL3 retired
instructions and the same CPL3 syscall journal. The series scenario outcome was
`passed`. The automatic strict comparator returned `matches=false` (process
exit 1), with unexplained `machine_observations` and
`ordered_uart_bytes` differences after nonce normalization.

| Run | #PF / #GP(0) | RDTSC `[CPL0,CPL1,CPL2,CPL3]` | PIT 0x61 / 0x42 | PM reads | IRQ0 edges / delivered | Quanta | Halt idle ns | Virtual ns |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 0001 | 33 / 1 | `[34443005, 0, 0, 0]` | 1 / 16,672 | 230 | 34,803 / 34,808 | 34,568,783 | 1,704,017 | 37,461,612,015 |
| 0002 | 33 / 1 | `[34459916, 0, 0, 0]` | 1 / 16,672 | 230 | 34,820 / 34,825 | 34,585,645 | 1,389,172 | 37,478,208,170 |

The aggregate `#PF` count is equal in this pair; the earlier 35/34 difference
did not recur here. This N=2 series did not collect per-event execution sidecars,
so it does not identify which faults changed or establish that the prior
startup-stack write fault was prevented. The different cmdline is a diagnostic
intervention, and the result does not establish causation or acceptance.

RDTSC totals differ by 16,911, all counted at CPL0. The virtual-time residual
(`virtual_ns - retired - halt_idle_ns - PM_reads * 1,000`) is 34,459,678,000 ns
and 34,476,589,000 ns; each equals `(RDTSC + PIT 0x61 reads + PIT 0x42 reads) *
1,000 ns`. The residual difference is therefore 16,911,000 ns. IRQ0 edges and
delivered IRQs differ by 17, quanta by 16,862, and halt idle by -314,845 ns.
These remain strict machine-observation differences.

After nonce and printk timestamp removal, UART still differs: the embedded
`audit(0.141:1)` line moves relative to adjacent output, `sched_clock` reports
different calibration values, and the terminal panic traces contain different
optional frames. No UART or machine-observation normalizer was changed.

